  "exact_same_site_and_allele_proof_plan": [
    "Before any observed native work, root separately registers a tiny CPU native qualification using the exact pinned Relate and RelateFileFormats binaries, guards and source-bound caps. No commands are run by this audit.",
    "Synthetic input must contain all-ancestral and all-derived40-haplotype rows at first, interior and last sites, heterozygous phase, ancestral-ALT orientation, several polymorphic vectors, fractional tip ages, nonuniform map knots, and duplicate-coordinate negative control. An all-constant separate case tests algorithm edge behavior.",
    "Do not alter v2 inputs. Require2074 .haps rows, same2074 native .mut identities/positions/order, no duplicates/rescue/drop/intersection. Count both constant classes and retain all277 actual monomorphic rows. Native input sample/age/map files must match admitted v2 bytes.",
    "Require40 flagged sample nodes in exact qualified haplotype insertion order. Verify IDs/roster, exact source calBP/28 age join and the frozen serialization policy. Parse every .anc age and reject missing/zero fallback, not merely a plausible range.",
    "Require2074 tskit sites at exact raw local bp1 positions. Decode every variant for all40 sample nodes without allele-index assumptions, reject missing values, and compare all82960 biological nucleotides in site/haplotype order to the independently verified v2 haps/source vectors. Require each of277 constant vectors, ancestry orientation and phase order exactly. Inspect every flipped/multiple-branch row.",
    "Record raw .anc/.mut/.trees hashes, all site/vector/order digests and a complete raw edge-interval union. Every one of2074 sites must be covered by a finite chronological tree carrying all40 samples. Do not silently repair converter time changes.",
    "Keep exact affine coordinate identity x0=absolute_POS_bp1-20000001=haps_POS_bp1-1. Raw converter sites use x0+1. Report native first0 and last+1 support separately from requested raw interval[1,10000001), including the artificial left1bp and any terminal unsupported flank. No claim of full10Mb coverage follows from map endpoints or last retained site.",
    "Do not reuse the generic 280-haplotype/2Mb runner: it filters monomorphic rows, assumes uniform map and strict1e-9 dates, then clips/rebases support. Any later coordinate adapter must preserve all2074 site vectors and native edge support, expose unsupported span, keep fixed normalization caveats and obtain a separate frozen policy.",
    "Only after tiny exact-binary qualification and an all-sites observed proof may root consider lifting the monomorphic-specific blocker. Other native/admission/date/chronology gates remain separate."
  ],
  "fractional_tip_age_policy": {
    "additional_native_tip_rule": "Each binary sample node must equal the corresponding parsed .anc age, with at most1 double ULP for qualified parser differences. Never widen tolerance from observed mismatch.",
    "chosen_path": "Finalize .anc %f then direct binary ConvertToTreeSequence; avoid text-table export and DumpStream",
    "expected_native_tip": "parse_double(format(original_age_generations, .6f)) under C locale and qualified round-to-nearest",
    "input_basis": "Original source calBP1950 /28, exact .17g bytes, no rounding/recent-date offset/clamp",
    "lineage_chronology_rule": "Compare parsed .anc branch-derived times and converter output, report every converter adjustment, require strict parent>child and no unreviewed repair. Do not overwrite tip dates after inference.",
    "old_1e_minus9_absolute_rule": "Not source-compatible with arbitrary six-decimal age export",
    "scope": "Tip serialization only; no universal tolerance for float internal-node dates or tree chronology",
    "source_to_native_bound_generations": "0.5e-6 + 8*ulp(original_age_generations), rtol=0",
    "status": "proposed_source_derived_policy_requires_root_freeze_and_actual_native_qualification"
  },
